<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suppiluliuma I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1344–1322 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suppiluliuma I was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> who reigned c. 1344–1322 BCE. He expanded Hittite power into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a>. He <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-sack-of-washukanni">sacked Washukanni</a> and installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shattiwaza">Shattiwaza</a> as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i.jpg" alt="Suppiluliuma I" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sémhur; derivative work by Ikonact · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Hittite_rule_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
